neath it.", "I put a small brass washer under the workshop stool this morning, but now all four legs look level and I cannot find the washer.", "I remember winding the workshop clock before breakfast, but now I cannot tell whether the extra ticking began this morning or yesterday.", "I left the little winding key in the workshop an hour ago. I remember the click of brass against tin, but not which tin.", "Yesterday I set a second-hand on the paper near the window to dry its oil, but there are several brass hands on that paper now.", "I remember scraping the dried oil from a brass plate this morning, but I cannot remember whether I did it before or after fitting the spring.", "I remember putting the spare spring in the chipped saucer, but the saucer is empty and there are two chipped bowls by the bench.", "The kettle has started to whistle, but I am still counting the screws in a shallow tray.", "The workshop broom has left a pale stripe of brass dust beside the door, and a customer is due in ten minutes.", "The workshop stool gives a short squeak whenever I shift my weight, and I have a brass shim beside the bench.", "At the market, I need one spool of black thread, but all eight spools look nearly identical.", "A tiny splinter from the bench catches in the pad of my thumb while I fit a spring by hand.", "Steam rolls from the kettle lid and catches the bare skin of my wrist while I reach for the tea.", "The heater coughs and releases a hot smell of old dust that makes my throat tighten.", "A drop of watch oil lands on the raw edge of my fingertip while I clean a brass wheel.", "The bench hinge has worked loose again. Replacing it would erase the shallow wear marks around the screws, but leaving it means another jar of screws may wander overnight.", "A visiting apprentice asks how long I intend to keep polishing a watch tooth that has already been polished twice.", "A neighbor leaning through the doorway asks why there are three little brass wheels drying on the window ledge.", "A small ceramic lid no longer sits flat. I can warm it over the lamp, or press it against the flat bench board and leave it overnight.", "There is one strip of fine abrasive paper, and I need it either to smooth a cracked bowl’s rim or to clean oil from a tiny wheel.", "I fit the tiny wheel into the movement, but it grinds and will not turn. When I tilt the watch, one pin stays behind and catches in the teeth.", "An hour ago I set a small brass wheel beside the blue-lidded oil tin. Now there are two blue-lidded tins on the bench, and I remember the reach, but not the lid.", "Yesterday I put the spare spring in a chipped saucer. Today the saucer is empty, though there are two chipped saucers near the bench and both have a brown ring inside.", "I remember winding the workshop clock before breakfast. Since then, the bench clock has gained a tick, but I cannot tell whether that happened this morning or yesterday.", "I left a folded strip of brass shim on the stool seat this morning. The stool seat is bare, but I remember a square of blue paper under it.", "I remember setting a tiny washer on the window ledge beside the dried leaf. The washer is gone, and so is the leaf, though a pale green speck remains in the sill groove.", "I remember cleaning the second-hand before fitting the spring, but I cannot remember whether the dry scrape came before or after the spring was seated. The plate has two oil marks.", "The kettle has whistled for half a minute, but I am still counting the little screws in a shallow tin.", "A loaf of bread has gone stale on the workbench. I have one hard heel, some soft crust, and enough broth to soak it in.", "At the market, I need one spool of black thread. Eight nearly identical spools are stacked beside the till, and the shopkeeper has gone to fetch change.", "While turning a broken brass fragment between finger and thumb, its sharp rim opens a thin line across my thumb pad.", "Steam rolls from the kettle lid and catches the bare skin of my wrist while I reach for the tea cup.", "A splinter from the bench catches in the pad of my thumb while I fit a spring by hand. The spring is still waiting beside the movement.", "A heel of bread has gone stale on the workbench. I have one hard crust, a soft middle, and enough broth to soak it in."]

